# SECRETS.md (template)

Copy to `SECRETS.md` and fill in. That filename is gitignored — it is a local
reference for setting up a new workstation or cloud agent, never committed.

**Do not paste secret values into this file in the repo, into chat, or into a
pull request.** The QuickBooks refresh token in particular grants access to the
company's books.

---

## Cloudflare Access service token

Gates `qbo.webpixelpro.com`. Created in Zero Trust → Access → Service Auth.

| Field | Where it goes |
| --- | --- |
| Client ID (ends `.access`) | `CF-Access-Client-Id` header |
| Client Secret | `CF-Access-Client-Secret` header |

- **Cursor desktop:** in `.cursor/mcp.json`, as `headers` entries.
- **Cursor cloud agents:** as `CF_ACCESS_CLIENT_ID` / `CF_ACCESS_CLIENT_SECRET`
  environment variables on the agent. Local `mcp.json` is not read in the cloud.
  Secrets are injected at VM boot, so an already-running agent will not see a
  newly added one — start a fresh agent.

Prefer a token dedicated to QuickBooks over reusing AdLoop's, so revoking one
does not disturb the other.

### Rotation

Re-issue in Zero Trust, update the desktop config and the cloud agent env vars,
then delete the old token. Symptom of a stale token is `403` on authenticated
calls while the unauthenticated `OPTIONS` preflight still returns `200`.

---

## Intuit app credentials

From the app's *Keys & Credentials* tab at developer.intuit.com. Sandbox and
production have **separate pairs** — record which is in use.

| Value | Lives on the server in |
| --- | --- |
| Client ID | `~/.qbo/tokens.env` → `QUICKBOOKS_CLIENT_ID` |
| Client Secret | `~/.qbo/tokens.env` → `QUICKBOOKS_CLIENT_SECRET` |
| Refresh token | `~/.qbo/tokens.env` → `QUICKBOOKS_REFRESH_TOKEN` |
| Realm (company) ID | `~/.qbo/tokens.env` → `QUICKBOOKS_REALM_ID` |

The refresh token **rotates on every refresh** and is rewritten in place, so the
value here goes stale immediately. Record the *company* and *environment* it
belongs to rather than trying to keep the token itself current.

### Expiry

Refresh tokens lapse after roughly **100 days**, silently, until a tool call
fails. Record the handshake date and set a reminder at ~90 days.

| Field | Value |
| --- | --- |
| Environment | sandbox / production |
| Company (realm) | |
| Last handshake | |
| Renew by | |

